    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 39 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**, including the four rewritten duplicate-detection checkpoints (Cp03 telephone, Cp10 household, Cp11 shared-household, Cp25 email) and the new Cp28 identity-key test.\n\n## Summary\n\nConsolidated all owner duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey`.\n\n**The key** \u2014 `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + householdId`:\n- `mapper/IdentityKey.java` \u2014 single source of truth deriving the key from an `Owner` (empty segments for a missing email/householdId).\n- Added an `identityKey` read-only field to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` and a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression in `OwnerMapper`, so the key is returned on both `POST` and `GET`.\n\n**The single rejection rule**:\n- `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique.java` \u2014 rejects with 409 (`DuplicateIdentityException` \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityHandler`, `errors: [\"identityKey\"]`) only when a new owner's *whole* identityKey equals an existing owner's.\n- Placed in `owners.POST.yml` *after* `assignHousehold` (so the built owner's `householdId` is settled) and *before* `save` (so the new owner isn't yet in `findAll()`).\n\n**Removed** the three old separate checks and their machinery: `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique`, `CheckOwnerEmailUnique`, `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique`, their `Duplicate{Telephone,Email,Household}Exception`/`Handler` classes, and the three escalation YAMLs \u2014 and pulled those three steps out of the pipeline.\n\nBecause the telephone is part of the key, two members of one household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now get distinct keys and are both allowed (Cp11), while a full-identity repeat still collides with 409 (Cp03/Cp10/Cp25/Cp28).\n\nNote: `POST /api/owners` requires the OfficeFloor Spring Boot starter to actually serve these YAML pipelines at runtime; without it the YAML files are inert (per AGENTS.md). The test suite exercises the pipeline as wired.",
